# tug support bundle

Diagnostic evidence about `{{.Target}}`{{if and .Namespace (not .IsNamespace)}} in namespace `{{.Namespace}}`{{end}} on cluster
`{{.Cluster}}`, collected by tug {{.Version}} at {{.Created}}. Events and
current logs cover the {{.Since}} before that{{if .LogsTail}}; each log keeps at most its last
{{.LogsTail}} lines{{end}}.

**Review it before you share it.** Redaction removes the credentials tug can
recognise. It cannot know everything your applications treat as private.
{{- if .Problems}}

Some things could not be collected: `manifest.json` lists them under
`problems`.
{{- end}}

## What is in it

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `manifest.json` | Every other file, its size, where it came from and how many values were redacted from it; how the bundle was collected; and anything tug could not collect. |
| `why/` | `tug why` of {{if .IsNamespace}}each workload in the namespace{{else}}the target{{end}}, as JSON: findings, pods, conditions and recent warnings. |
| `tree/` | `tug tree` of the same, as JSON: what it owns, with the health of each part. |
| `objects/<namespace>/<resource>/<name>.yaml` | {{if .IsNamespace}}Everything in the namespace{{else}}The target and what it owns{{end}}, as the API server returned it, redacted. Cluster-scoped objects are under `_cluster`. |
| `events.json` | Events about those objects in the window, oldest first. |
| `logs/<namespace>/<pod>/<container>.log` | Each container's log over the window, with timestamps. `<container>.previous.log` is the end of its previous run, when it has restarted. Up to {{.MaxLogPods}} pods, those not ready first. |
| `nodes/<node>.yaml` | The conditions, capacity, taints and versions of the nodes the pods run on. |
| `cluster/version.json` | The API server's version. |
| `cluster/api-resources.json` | The resources the API server serves, custom resources included. |
| `doctor.json` | `tug doctor`'s checks of tug's setup and of the cluster. |
{{- if or .Include .Exclude}}

Only some kinds of object were collected:{{if .Include}} those of `--include {{range $i, $k := .Include}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}{{$k}}{{end}}`{{end}}{{if .Exclude}}{{if .Include}}, and{{end}} not those of `--exclude {{range $i, $k := .Exclude}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}{{$k}}{{end}}`{{end}}.
{{- end}}

## What was redacted

Every redacted value reads `<redacted>`.

- **Secrets**: metadata only. tug copies each Secret from the metadata API,
  which serves no data, so no Secret's data is in this bundle.
- **Environment variables**: the `value` of every variable in an `env` list,
  in pods, pod templates and custom resources. Names and `valueFrom`
  references, which say where a value comes from, are kept.
- **ConfigMaps**: every value under `data` and `binaryData`. The keys are kept.
- **The `kubectl.kubernetes.io/last-applied-configuration` annotation** on
  every object: it is a copy of the object as it was applied, a Secret's data
  included.
- **Fields named like a credential**, such as `password`, `token` or `apiKey`,
  and the values of name and value pairs named so, such as Helm parameters.
  Fields that only name or point to one, such as `secretName`, are kept.
- **In logs, events and every other string**: bearer and basic credentials,
  passwords in URLs, JSON Web Tokens, PEM private keys, AWS access key IDs,
  GitHub, GitLab and Slack tokens, and assignments such as `password=...`,
  `--api-token=...` or `"apiKey": "..."`.
{{- if .Patterns}}
- **{{.Patterns}} pattern{{if gt .Patterns 1}}s{{end}} given with `--redact-pattern`**, wherever {{if gt .Patterns 1}}they match{{else}}it matches{{end}}. The
  patterns themselves are not in the bundle.
{{- end}}

`metadata.managedFields`, which only says which client set which field, is
left out.

Not redacted: names, namespaces, labels, other annotations, images, IP
addresses and host names, and the rest of each log line. File names come from
object names.

## How to review it

Unpack it, which makes the directory `{{.Name}}`, and search it:

```sh
tar -xzf {{.Archive}}
grep -rniE 'passw|secret|token|bearer|api.?key|://[^/ ]+:[^/ ]+@' {{.Name}}
```

Read the logs above all: applications log in formats of their own, and a
credential in a format tug does not know is left as it is. `manifest.json`
counts the redactions in each file.

To leave more out, collect the bundle again with `--redact-pattern '<regex>'`,
or without whole kinds with `--exclude <kind>`. `--preview` lists the files
that would be written, with their sizes, and writes nothing.
